> > I am not sure if I understand your question right. Nethack's 'map' size
> > is obviously fixed and will not change dynamically with terminal
> > character resolution. Is it that you want more text 'history' lines? I
> > don't think most ports support this.
> Some amendments:
> 1. If the LINES environment variable is set appropriately before unix
> nethack starts, then you can indeed use the larger screen size for long
> inventory listings, options listings, ^P history, etc. Also works with
> the win32 tty port (which will read the number of lines from the actual
> console window size, not the LINES variable).
[...]
> 3. When you set the terminal size in putty *before connecting*, NAO
> *will* read the LINES variable supplied by putty and use it. So you'll
> get the long inventory listings etc. as described in 1. (I just tried
> this, and it works.)

